/-! 1687. Equal forces: errors at proportional times share one Lemma X coefficient. -/
/-! Witness: 1687.
Source: docs/m1/NATP00077.xml
SHA-256: 57a8eb4ae7307faed09e2ae572a4975ea2011e679ce52e6ad2413028c424dffa
URL: https://www.newtonproject.ox.ac.uk/view/texts/diplomatic/NATP00077#par29
Anchor URLs: NATP00077.par29 = https://www.newtonproject.ox.ac.uk/view/texts/diplomatic/NATP00077#par29
Proof-step correspondence: Each error is a function of its own vanishing time. Equal forces similarly applied are represented by one Lemma X coefficient `c` for both errors, a supplied premise; the similar figures enter only through it and through the fixed time proportion `r`. The edition's Lemma X reconstruction gives each error divided by the square of its time the ultimate value `c`, with the second error read at the proportional time `r * t`. For positive `c`, two normalized errors with one ultimate value express "ut quadrata temporum ... quam proxime"; the ultimate ratio of the two errors themselves is not formed. The places reached without the forces and the similarity of the figures are not constructed.
